---
import { getRelativeLocaleUrl } from "astro:i18n";
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "@/components/Header.astro";
import Breadcrumb from "@/components/Breadcrumb.astro";
import Main from "@/components/Main.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/Footer.astro";
import config from "@/config";

const locale = Astro.currentLocale ?? config.site.lang;
---

<Layout
  title={`Prompt-to-Ontology — ${config.site.title}`}
  description="A practical checklist from the Pet Food reference: define types and rules, review imports, inspect evidence, and keep agent suggestions reversible."
>
  <Header />
  <Breadcrumb />

  <Main pageTitle="Prompt-to-Ontology" class="app-prose">
    <p class="text-muted-foreground text-lg">
      A checklist drawn from the Pet Food reference implementation: decide what
      the data means, make rule results inspectable, and keep graph changes
      under review.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">The starting question</h2>
    <p>
      Before an agent queries a graph, someone has to decide which objects and
      relationships the source data represents, which rules apply, and what
      happens when the evidence is incomplete. Those are product decisions as
      much as modeling decisions.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">From data to a reviewable graph</h2>
    <ol class="mt-2 list-inside list-decimal space-y-3">
      <li>
        <strong>Declare the types</strong> — Which object and relationship types exist
        in this domain? Define them in a versioned schema.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Profile the data</strong> — Inspect the columns, missing values, identifiers,
        and candidate mappings before import.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Review the import plan</strong> — Which candidates can be applied,
        which require a person to resolve a mapping, and what gets rejected?
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Define rules and evidence</strong> — Record what a rule used and distinguish
        triggered, passed, not evaluable, and not applicable.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Bound agent tools</strong> — Which objects, relationships, and rule
        results can the agent inspect? Where do its suggestions wait for review?
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Plan for correction</strong> — Can a reviewer inspect a trace, compare
        graph snapshots, and roll back a mistaken change?
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Pet Food example</h2>
    <p>The public demo tests this checklist with one sample domain:</p>
    <ul class="mt-2 space-y-2">
      <li>
        <strong>Schema:</strong> object types, link types, constraints, rules, and
        actions declared in YAML
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Import:</strong> sample CSV profiling and a reviewable plan before
        graph writes
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Runtime:</strong> typed objects, relationships, rule evidence, and
        an Analyst Agent trace
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Governance:</strong> human approval, snapshots, diffs, and rollback
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The example is inspectable, but it has not been validated beyond Pet Food.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Checks before calling it useful</h2>
    <ul class="mt-2 space-y-2">
      <li>
        Can a reviewer see the source and mapping behind an imported object?
      </li>
      <li>
        Does a missing value produce “not evaluable” rather than an unsupported
        pass result?
      </li>
      <li>
        Can an agent proposal be rejected, and can an applied graph change be
        inspected and reversed?
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="border-border mt-8 rounded-lg border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Related</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          href={getRelativeLocaleUrl(locale, "projects/prompt-to-ontology")}
          class="text-accent hover:underline"
        >
          Prompt-to-Ontology Project
        </a>
        <a
          href={getRelativeLocaleUrl(locale, "playbook/agent-product-design")}
          class="text-accent hover:underline"
        >
          Agent Product Design
        </a>
        <a
          href={getRelativeLocaleUrl(locale, "playbook")}
          class="text-accent hover:underline"
        >
          Methodology Index
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
